{"lines":[{"c":1,"t":"Test 2","h":0.014593194719612845,"y":0.04941860483360061,"w":0.06160164515177409,"x":0.086242298475143434},{"h":0.017831426524834604,"y":0.094281961139328629,"x":0.43937479685849479,"c":1,"t":"READING","w":0.13357073465983071},{"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.086242296768350102,"y":0.15693215341306144,"h":0.016032962742808299,"c":1,"w":0.30800821940104167},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","y":0.19176752542259612,"w":0.81741877237955718,"h":0.019990599190591096,"x":0.086164096109102667,"c":1},{"h":0.01967601494803195,"y":0.20957914617368534,"x":0.085897536986132908,"t":"Passage 1 below.","w":0.1730422719319662,"c":1},{"x":0.26283366543253728,"t":"The Industrial Revolution in Britain","y":0.2513274335593737,"w":0.48459960937500002,"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1},{"h":0.01606554858452458,"x":0.086242293419394017,"y":0.28924418616209513,"t":"The Industrial Revolution began in Britain in the mid-1700s and by the 1830s and 1840s","w":0.80287475585937496,"c":1},{"h":0.017502744218944488,"y":0.30668604653515452,"t":"had spread to many other parts of the world, including the United States. In Britain, it was a","x":0.08418891894946863,"w":0.83162216186523441,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.82546203613281244,"y":0.32412790747124576,"t":"period when a largely rural, agrarian* society was transformed into an industrialised, urban","h":0.018939939290724794,"x":0.086242287782799465},{"y":0.34302325592953697,"t":"one. Goods that had once been crafted by hand started to be produced in mass quantities","w":0.82135523478190109,"x":0.08624230037449318,"h":0.015988371857499684,"c":1},{"t":"by machines in factories, thanks to the invention of steam power and the introduction of","c":1,"x":0.08418892434367431,"y":0.36046511630299727,"w":0.80082132975260412,"h":0.017441860412777621},{"w":0.82135523478190098,"y":0.37787610630701196,"h":0.018926218758642088,"c":1,"t":"new machines and manufacturing techniques in textiles, iron-making and other industries.","x":0.08418891240330803},{"y":0.41563421833928094,"h":0.016051828052441985,"t":"The foundations of the Industrial Revolution date back to the early 1\/00s, when the","c":1,"x":0.086242311909078731,"w":0.78439422607421871},{"y":0.43021519048638768,"t":"English inventor Thomas Newcomen designed the first modern steam engine. Called the","h":0.017685478908122443,"c":1,"w":0.81939885457356765,"x":0.086193352196118456},{"c":1,"w":0.83983571370442711,"h":0.018992247904999759,"y":0.44767441886567583,"x":0.084188915093371772,"t":"'atmospheric steam engine', Newcomen's invention was originally used to power machines"},{"h":0.020725936664592437,"t":"that pumped water out of mines. In the 1760s, the Scottish engineer James Watt","y":0.46605646900805953,"c":1,"x":0.086174358685797384,"w":0.76196523030598962},{"h":0.021654980864848405,"c":1,"y":0.48268080420179382,"t":"started to adapt one of Newcomen's models, and succeeded in making it far more","w":0.77433110555013018,"x":0.086140021133739988},{"h":0.015988371857499573,"x":0.086242306264195087,"t":"efficient. Watt later worked with the English manufacturer Matthew Boulton to invent a","c":1,"w":0.80698150634765631,"y":0.50290697685968322},{"c":1,"h":0.015988371857499684,"t":"new steam engine driven by both the forward and backward strokes of the piston, while","x":0.084188899701243727,"y":0.5218023256969907,"w":0.82546203613281255},{"t":"the gear mechanism it was connected to produced rotary motion. It was a key innovation","w":0.83778233846028649,"h":0.01747444569185419,"c":1,"x":0.084188916067597958,"y":0.53775811224709269},{"t":"that would allow steam power to spread across British industries.","y":0.55663716786357886,"w":0.61806981404622396,"h":0.016037250620073995,"x":0.08418891218604263,"c":1},{"y":0.59144542746442896,"w":0.81108830769856766,"t":"The demand for coal, which was a relatively cheap energy source, grew rapidly during","h":0.017699115044247815,"x":0.086242293674036713,"c":1},{"w":0.82560119628906248,"h":0.019383530068186605,"x":0.084121725363690697,"c":1,"t":"the Industrial Revolution, as it was needed to run not only the factories used to produce","y":0.60774204618050087},{"y":0.62614626011920338,"c":1,"h":0.019309815263326202,"t":"manufactured goods, but also steam-powered transportation. In the early 1800s, the","w":0.79477615356445308,"x":0.086181856598606527},{"t":"English engineer Richard Trevithick built a steam-powered locomotive, and by 1830","y":0.64534883723318859,"w":0.78850102742513017,"c":1,"h":0.017483021446385583,"x":0.086242299326449182},{"h":0.015988371857499573,"c":1,"t":"goods and passengers were being transported between the industrial centres of","x":0.084188923043490904,"y":0.66279069778988986,"w":0.75975357055664061},{"h":0.015988371857499684,"c":1,"w":0.79055440266927091,"y":0.68168604662728027,"t":"Manchester and Liverpool. In addition, steam-powered boats and ships were widely","x":0.084188917658120768},{"y":0.69764011825147498,"w":0.68377822875976557,"t":"used to carry goods along Britain's canals as well as across the Atlantic.","h":0.017476160617704517,"c":1,"x":0.086242301821349274},{"x":0.08624228778364379,"y":0.73392330362321778,"w":0.82546203613281244,"h":0.017530184720469855,"c":1,"t":"Britain had produced textiles like wool, linen and cotton, for hundreds of years, but prior"},{"h":0.022231967892267002,"c":1,"y":0.74826382504471334,"w":0.83588175455729163,"t":"to the Industrial Revolution, the British textile business was a true 'cottage industry', with","x":0.084112893391091834},{"c":1,"w":0.8215694681803386,"h":0.020935380423666827,"t":"the work performed in small workshops or even homes by individual spinners, weavers","y":0.76727439602567338,"x":0.084087221821775984},{"c":1,"y":0.78779069769793708,"t":"and dyers. Starting in the mid-1700s, innovations like the spinning jenny and the power","x":0.086242306784598766,"w":0.8234086100260416,"h":0.017519036577162805},{"h":0.016006379704208151,"t":"loom made weaving cloth and spinning yarn and thread much easier. With these","x":0.084188904062112518,"y":0.80523255824327189,"c":1,"w":0.76180699666341145},{"x":0.086197830898794806,"w":0.83583409627278638,"c":1,"y":0.82259522030331367,"t":"machines, relatively little labour was required to produce cloth, and the new, mechanised","h":0.01890717678013798},{"x":0.084188917656518258,"y":0.8415697675572984,"t":"textile factories that opened around the country were quickly able to meet customer","w":0.79055440266927079,"h":0.015988371857499684,"c":1},{"t":"demand for cloth both at home and abroad.","c":1,"w":0.41478439331054684,"x":0.086242300179503961,"y":0.85899705002485627,"h":0.016002949852507387},{"x":0.084107904344342427,"w":0.41083905537923182,"h":0.013238208061825962,"c":1,"t":"* agrarian: relating to the land, especially the use of land for farming","y":0.89966805795834459},{"h":0.013081394746943587,"w":0.028747431437174481,"y":0.92296511652055568,"c":1,"x":0.08418891250616542,"t":"40"},{"x":0.51176470218665204,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.45294118245442705,"y":0.94166666659226195,"h":0.04166666666666663,"c":1}],"h":3390,"w":2400}